# Cold-reader audit reports and other working notes are written straight into
# this repository, because a reviewing instance is given access to the published
# tree only — it has nowhere else to put them. They are working material, not
# publication: they must never be committed here.
#
# This file is the mechanism for that. It replaces a rule that used to live in
# someone's attention: three times in one day an internal report landed inside
# this clone and was caught, each time, by the privacy gate immediately before a
# push. A guard that fires at the last line is a working guard, but it is the
# wrong place for a rule that can simply be made structural.
K*/
_reports/
_notes/
*.local.md

# Build artefacts of the Lean sources shipped under src/lean/
.lake/
build/
